{
    "word": "undissembled",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "c461a9eb-df0c-31f4-9bb1-89a7181acd62",
                "word": "undissembled",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "39589529-7731-4146-a3f3-4e07cc56dd57",
                        "entry_id": "c461a9eb-df0c-31f4-9bb1-89a7181acd62",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more undissembled"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "c1a204e6-309f-4045-bff0-b12ef0caed22",
                        "entry_id": "c461a9eb-df0c-31f4-9bb1-89a7181acd62",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most undissembled"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bdddd941-60fd-3723-a536-7f4fca524265",
                        "entry_id": "c461a9eb-df0c-31f4-9bb1-89a7181acd62",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Not dissembled.",
                            "Not concealed or disguised; evident, obvious."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "75b0fa22-8cdd-4bd7-a63d-9c60b92126f4",
                                "sense_id": "bdddd941-60fd-3723-a536-7f4fca524265",
                                "text": "She [Delilah] purpos'd to betray me, and (vvhich vvas vvorſe / Then undiſſembl'd hate) vvith vvhat contempt / She ſought to make me Traytor to my ſelf; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0c2da498-a180-4fa6-8642-ecb300897a26",
                                "sense_id": "bdddd941-60fd-3723-a536-7f4fca524265",
                                "text": "Emilia, vvarmed by ſo many concurring incentives, in favour of the man ſhe loved, abated conſiderably of her vvonted reſerve, liſtened to his proteſtations vvith undiſſembled pleaſure, and in the confidence of her ſatisfaction, even ovvned him abſolute maſter of her affections."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "08032778-6a31-4dae-b7bd-6f65d9461d1b",
                                "sense_id": "bdddd941-60fd-3723-a536-7f4fca524265",
                                "text": "He paid me the moſt high-flovvn compliments, and frequently and forcibly ſeized my hand, though I repeatedly, and vvith undiſſembled anger, drevv it back."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dd475f1f-1ae2-4b34-94df-96682fee99eb",
                                "sense_id": "bdddd941-60fd-3723-a536-7f4fca524265",
                                "text": "The earnestness of his thanks called drops to the eyes of the worthy clergyman, who was doubly interested in the cause for which he had volunteered his services, by observing the genuine and undissembled feelings of his young friend."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e8f21e6a-ffd8-40f9-8dd6-b4b01c5171f6",
                                "sense_id": "bdddd941-60fd-3723-a536-7f4fca524265",
                                "text": "The only truth, that continued to give Mr. Dimmesdale a real existence on this earth, was the anguish in his inmost soul, and the undissembled expression of it in his aspect."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "804d709c-4236-33e3-8e21-18ea1fb39e5d",
                        "entry_id": "c461a9eb-df0c-31f4-9bb1-89a7181acd62",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Not dissembled.",
                            "Not dissimulated or feigned; genuine, unfaked."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "122a0200-27db-43ca-b726-cfb22b859d7f",
                                "sense_id": "804d709c-4236-33e3-8e21-18ea1fb39e5d",
                                "text": "There is a Reall undiſſembled Faith, vvhich yet is not juſtifying or ſaving. VVho can deny that?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a00d8fee-1490-4adf-91e3-4702a0461c61",
                                "sense_id": "804d709c-4236-33e3-8e21-18ea1fb39e5d",
                                "text": "I ſavv the reſpectful Dovvncaſt of his Eye, vvhen you catcht him gazing at you during the Muſick: He, I vvarrant, vvas ſurpriz'd, as if he had been taken ſtealing your VVatch. O! the undiſſembled Guilty Look!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "871a8150-b2af-4c55-bf61-fb43f181f407",
                                "sense_id": "804d709c-4236-33e3-8e21-18ea1fb39e5d",
                                "text": "I write to-night, lest my stay in Cornwall might make my delay appear tedious to the dear and deserving object of my most undissembled love. Oh my Sarah, had I as much proof of that I love Jesus Christ, as I have of my love to you, I should prize it more than rubies!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4d29c586-afec-43b2-a88c-4178d46bc844",
                                "sense_id": "804d709c-4236-33e3-8e21-18ea1fb39e5d",
                                "text": "[H]is [Jesus's] whole life, […] was full of grace and truth: that is, conspicuously distinguished by the most amiable condescension, and benignity of disposition and manners, and by the most undissembled and inviolable sincerity."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
